arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a logistics shipment tracking Blazor Web App. The project has already been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-ed803021ff864357bb296a13f95242f1/ShipmentTracker/` using `dotnet new blazor -int Auto -ai -au Individual`.

## Project Structure
- **ShipmentTracker/** (server project) — hosts app, API endpoints, EF Core
- **ShipmentTracker.Client/** — all interactive UI components (Auto global mode)
- Auth is configured with ASP.NET Core Identity + SQLite
- Global InteractiveAuto mode is set in App.razor

## Requirements
1. Dispatchers view a list of shipments with status and destination
2. Customers check their shipment status and estimated delivery
3. Every page has interactive controls
4. Staff and customers authenticate with individual accounts

## Implementation Plan

### Step 1: Create shared models in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Models/ShipmentDto.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CarrierName { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Notes { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public class ShipmentStatusUpdate
{
    public string Status { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Notes { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}

public class TrackingResult
{
    public bool Found { get; set; }
    public ShipmentDto? Shipment { get; set; }
    public string Message { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### Step 2: Create service interface in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/IShipmentService.cs`:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentAsync(int id);
    Task<TrackingResult> TrackShipmentAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment);
    Task UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatusUpdate update);
}
```

### Step 3: Create HttpClient-based implementation in `.Client` project

Create `ShipmentTracker.Client/Services/ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;
using ShipmentTracker.Client.Models;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client.Services;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentAsync(int id)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>($"api/shipments/{id}");
    }

    public async Task<TrackingResult> TrackShipmentAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        return await http.GetFromJsonAsync<TrackingResult>($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}") 
            ?? new TrackingResult { Found = false, Message = "Unable to reach server." };
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>() ?? shipment;
    }

    public async Task UpdateStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatusUpdate update)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", update);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
    }
}
```

### Step 4: Register HttpClient and service in Client Program.cs

Edit `ShipmentTracker.Client/Program.cs` to add:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddScoped(sp => new HttpClient { BaseAddress = new Uri(builder.HostEnvironment.BaseAddress) });
builder.Services.AddScoped<IShipmentService, ShipmentHttpService>();
```
Add the needed usings.

### Step 5: Create EF entity in server project

Create `ShipmentTracker/Data/Shipment.cs`:
```csharp
using System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }

    [Required, MaxLength(50)]
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(200)]
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(200)]
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [Required, MaxLength(50)]
    public string Status { get; set; } = "Pending";

    [Required, MaxLength(256)]
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    public DateTime ShippedDate { get; set; }
    public DateTime EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }

    [MaxLength(200)]
    public string CarrierName { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    [MaxLength(1000)]
    public string Notes { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### Step 6: Update ApplicationDbContext

Edit `ShipmentTracker/Data/ApplicationDbContext.cs` to add DbSet and seed data:
```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.EntityFrameworkCore;
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public class ApplicationDbContext(DbContextOptions<ApplicationDbContext> options) : IdentityDbContext<ApplicationUser>(options)
{
